{#- Credentials band. August 27, 2026 — third revision, replaces trust-bar.njk.

    History, because two earlier shapes were wrong for reasons worth keeping:
      v1  name + explanatory note in a 3-column grid, directly under the hero.
          ~450px of body copy where a trust signal belongs.
      v2  one compact row of names, still under the hero. Better, but Iván's
          verdict was that the position itself was unnatural — a credential
          block is not what a visitor wants immediately after the headline.
      v3  this. A logo band, moved DOWN the page to sit after the testimonials
          and before the final CTA: athlete proof, then institutional proof,
          then the ask.

    Grouped by ISSUING BODY, not by credential. TrainingPeaks issued two of the
    five, and showing the TrainingPeaks mark twice in one row reads as a
    mistake. The band never restates a credential name — it references item ids
    and prints each item's `capt`, so _data/credentials.json `items` stays the
    single owner of the wording.                                              -#}
{%- set cr = credentials[lang] -%}
<section class="cred-band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label">{{ cr.label }}</span>
    <h2>{{ cr.h2 }}</h2>
    <p class="cred-band-lead">{{ cr.lead }}</p>
    <ul class="cred-band-list">
      {#- Rows come from _data/credentialsBand.js, which resolves each band
          row's item ids to their captions and joins them. credentials.json
          `items` stays the single owner of the wording. -#}
      {%- for row in credentialsBand[lang] %}
      <li class="cred-band-item">
        <span class="cred-band-logo cred-band-logo-{{ row.markType }}">
          <img src="{{ row.logo | v }}" alt="{{ row.org }} {{ cr.logoAltSuffix }}" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        </span>
        <span class="cred-band-capt">{{ row.capt }}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="cred-band-more"><a href="{{ cr.aboutHref }}">{{ cr.aboutLabel }} &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
